];
---

<Layout title="Waiver">
    <div class="container">
        <PageHeader title="Waiver" />

        <h2>PASSAGE GATHERING 2026 LIABILITY WAIVER, ASSUMPTION OF RISK, AND PARTICIPANT AGREEMENT</h2>
        <p>
            READ CAREFULLY BEFORE SIGNING. THIS IS A LEGALLY BINDING AGREEMENT THAT AFFECTS YOUR LEGAL RIGHTS. IT
            INCLUDES AN ASSUMPTION OF RISK, A RELEASE OF CLAIMS FOR ORDINARY NEGLIGENCE TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED
            BY ALABAMA LAW, AND A REQUIREMENT TO ATTEMPT MEDIATION BEFORE FILING A LAWSUIT.
        </p>

        <p>
            In consideration of being permitted to enter the property used for Passage Gathering 2026 (the “Facilities”)
            and to attend, participate in, or observe Passage Gathering 2026 (the “Event” or “Passage”), I agree as
            follows:
        </p>

        <h3>1. Eligibility, Age, and Legal Capacity</h3>
        <p>
            I represent and warrant that I am at least twenty-one (21) years old, that I have the legal capacity to
            enter into this Agreement, and that I am signing it voluntarily on my own behalf. I understand that Passage
            is an adults-only event and that this Agreement is not intended to be signed on behalf of a minor.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Definitions; Activities and Risks</h3>
        <p>
            “Activities” means all activities, programs, recreation, entertainment, camping, transportation, use of
            facilities, and other participation associated with or occurring at the Facilities or the Event, whether
            organized by FarmCamp, Gravity, independent entities, vendors, promoters, volunteers, participants, or
            others. Activities include, without limitation: hiking; camping; swimming; kayaking; fishing; boating and
            other water activities; dancing; biking and mountain biking; climbing, rappelling, zip lining, ropes courses
            and rope swings; inflatables; field and team-building games; archery, paintball, archery tag, BB-gun/riflery
            activities where offered; use of fire in designated or authorized activities; art installations;
            performances; theme camps; and use of roads, trails, pathways, parking areas, stairs, buildings, tents,
            campsites, pools, hot tubs, creeks, vehicles, golf carts, and other facilities or equipment.
        </p>
        <p>
            I understand that participation in or presence around the Activities involves inherent and other risks
            (“Risks”), known and unknown, foreseeable and unforeseeable, including without limitation:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                serious bodily injury, permanent disability, paralysis, illness, allergic reaction, property damage,
                economic loss, and death;
            </li>
            <li>
                falls, slips, trips, collisions, impacts, entanglement, drowning, immersion, high speeds, sudden stops,
                and becoming pinned or entrapped;
            </li>
            <li>
                weather, heat, cold, darkness or limited lighting, physical exertion, uneven or wet surfaces, natural
                and man-made obstacles, and remote conditions that may delay emergency response;
            </li>
            <li>
                equipment, structural, harness, line, helmet, vehicle, bicycle, watercraft, electrical, staging, art, or
                safety-equipment failure or malfunction;
            </li>
            <li>
                contact with other participants, staff, volunteers, vendors, vehicles, bicycles, equipment, projectiles,
                fire or flame effects, electrical music equipment, and other Event features;
            </li>
            <li>
                wildlife, animals, insects, reptiles, plants and natural features, including snakes, alligators,
                raccoons, mosquitoes, deer, boars, and similar hazards;
            </li>
            <li>
                acts or omissions of other persons, including negligent, reckless, violent, criminal, or otherwise
                unsafe conduct by third parties;
            </li>
            <li>
                exposure to communicable or infectious diseases, including influenza, COVID-19, and other illnesses; and
            </li>
            <li>
                other hazards associated with camping, recreation, live events, unfamiliar surroundings,
                participant-provided equipment, and activities not specifically listed above.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            I understand that the foregoing list is illustrative and not exhaustive. If at any time I believe conditions
            are unsafe or I am physically or otherwise unable to participate safely, I will stop participating
            immediately.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Knowing and Voluntary Assumption of Risk</h3>
        <p>
            I knowingly and voluntarily accept and assume all inherent Risks associated with attending Passage, entering
            or using the Facilities, and participating in the Activities. I choose to attend and participate despite
            those Risks and accept responsibility for injuries, losses, costs, or damages I may sustain from inherent
            Risks or from my own acts or omissions or the acts or omissions of third parties, subject to the limitations
            stated in Section 4 below.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Release and Waiver of Claims - Ordinary Negligence Only</h3>
        <p>
            For purposes of this Agreement, “Releasees” means FarmCamp, LLC, Gravity Events and Promotions, LLC, Passage
            Gathering, and each of their respective subsidiaries, affiliates, owners, officers, directors, employees,
            agents, volunteers, contractors, representatives, successors, and assigns.
        </p>

        <p>
            TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY ALABAMA LAW, I RELEASE, WAIVE, DISCHARGE, AND COVENANT NOT TO SUE THE
            RELEASEES FOR CLAIMS FOR PERSONAL INJURY, ILLNESS, DEATH, PROPERTY DAMAGE, LOSS, OR OTHER DAMAGES ARISING
            OUT OF OR RELATING TO MY ATTENDANCE AT PASSAGE, MY PRESENCE AT THE FACILITIES, OR MY PARTICIPATION IN THE
            ACTIVITIES, INCLUDING CLAIMS CAUSED IN WHOLE OR IN PART BY THE ORDINARY NEGLIGENCE OF A RELEASEE.
        </p>

        <p>
            This release is not intended to, and does not, release or waive any claim for wantonness, willful
            misconduct, intentional misconduct, or any other claim or liability that cannot lawfully be released or
            waived under applicable Alabama law. Nothing in this Agreement shall be construed to expand this release
            beyond what Alabama law permits.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Indemnification and Responsibility for My Conduct</h3>
        <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by Alabama law, I agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Releasees from
            third-party claims, losses, liabilities, damages, costs, and reasonable attorneys’ fees arising from my own
            acts or omissions, my violation of this Agreement or Event rules, or damage or injury I cause to another
            person or property. This indemnity is not intended to require me to indemnify a Releasee for wanton,
            willful, or intentional misconduct or for any liability that cannot lawfully be shifted or indemnified under
            Alabama law.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Health, Insurance, and Emergency Medical Treatment</h3>
        <p>
            I represent that I am physically and medically capable of safely attending the Event and participating in
            any Activities I choose to undertake, or that I will refrain from activities for which I am not capable. I
            understand that I am responsible for my own medical needs, medications, food, shelter, hydration, and other
            personal requirements. I certify that I have adequate insurance to cover injury or damage I may cause or
            suffer, or I agree to bear those costs myself.
        </p>

        <p>
            If I am unable to provide consent during a medical emergency, I authorize emergency medical treatment
            considered reasonably advisable for accident, injury, or illness occurring during Passage. I understand that
            the Releasees are not obligated to provide medical services. To the maximum extent permitted by Alabama law,
            the release in Section 4 applies to ordinary-negligence claims arising from the provision or attempted
            provision of emergency aid or medical assistance by a Releasee. The carve-out for wanton, willful, or
            intentional misconduct stated in Section 4 also applies here.
        </p>

        <h3>7. Participant Conduct, Safety Rules, and Removal</h3>
        <p>
            I agree to follow the Passage Gathering Code of Conduct, FarmCamp rules, posted signs, warnings, and
            instructions, and all lawful directions of Event and venue personnel. I understand that violation of this
            Agreement or Event rules may result in refusal of entry or immediate removal from the Event without a
            refund, except where a refund is required by the policy stated in Section 10 or by applicable law.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                FarmCamp is a drug-free environment. Possession, use, or distribution of illegal drugs is prohibited and
                may result in removal and/or referral to law enforcement.
            </li>

            <li>
                Firearms, ammunition, projectile weapons not expressly authorized as part of an Event Activity,
                fireworks, and explosives are prohibited at Passage and at FarmCamp, including in vehicles, subject to
                applicable law.
            </li>

            <li>Unauthorized sound equipment is prohibited.</li>

            <li>
                I will stay within established activity areas and obey restrictions concerning open water, pools, hot
                tubs, creeks, roads, trails, and other designated areas. I understand that swimming and other water
                activities are undertaken at my own risk and that a lifeguard may not be present.
            </li>

            <li>
                I will respect the Facilities, staff, volunteers, other attendees, and their property. Violence,
                threatening or disruptive behavior, theft, or intentional destruction of property may result in
                immediate removal and/or referral to law enforcement.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>8. Camping, Property, Vehicles, and Leave No Trace</h3>
        <p>
            I am responsible for my campsite and personal property. Passage is a Leave No Trace event. I will remove or
            properly dispose of trash and leave my campsite in substantially the same condition as I found it. I
            understand that I may be charged for cleanup or for damage I cause to the Facilities or the property of
            others.
        </p>
        <p>
            My vehicle must remain in designated parking areas except as authorized. To the maximum extent permitted by
            law, FarmCamp, Gravity, and other Releasees are not responsible for theft of or damage to vehicles or
            property left in or around vehicles, except to the extent arising from liability that cannot lawfully be
            released. Re-entry is subject to Event rules and prior approval where required.
        </p>
        <p>
            Camping access is governed by the pass purchased through the Shotgun platform. Attendees must comply with
            applicable check-in and check-out times. Early arrival requires any separately required Early Arrival Pass.
        </p>

        <h3>9. Third-Party Installations, Activities, and Participant Environment</h3>
        <p>
            I understand that art installations, theme camps, participant-provided structures, bicycles, motorized
            devices, tents, stages, performances, equipment, and other features may be installed, owned, operated, or
            controlled by third parties rather than by Passage Gathering, FarmCamp, or Gravity. I assume the inherent
            Risks associated with interacting with such features and with the acts or omissions of third parties.
        </p>
        <p>
            I understand that Passage is an adult-oriented interactive event and that I may encounter lawful behavior,
            artistic expression, costumes, nudity, or other content that I may find offensive. Subject to the Code of
            Conduct and applicable law, I am responsible for removing myself from areas or situations I do not wish to
            experience.
        </p>

        <h3>10. Tickets, Refunds, Cancellation, and Force Majeure</h3>
        <p>
            All ticket and camping-pass sales are final except as provided by the applicable policies established on the
            Shotgun ticketing platform or as otherwise required by law. The Event is intended to proceed rain or shine.
            If the Event is canceled, terminated early, postponed, or materially affected by force majeure, governmental
            action, weather, emergency, or other circumstances beyond Gravity’s reasonable control, any refund, credit,
            transfer, or other ticket remedy will be handled according to the policies established on the Shotgun
            ticketing platform. This Section 10 controls over any inconsistent statement concerning refunds or
            cancellation.
        </p>

        <h3>11. Photography, Recording, Image, Likeness, and Voice</h3>
        <p>
            By entering the Event, I grant Gravity permission to photograph, record, and use my image, likeness, and
            voice in live or recorded video, photographs, broadcasts, transmissions, or other reproductions of the
            Event, in media now known or later developed, for lawful promotional, archival, or Event-related purposes
            without compensation, subject to applicable law.
        </p>
        <p>
            If I photograph, film, or record participants, artwork, or activities at Passage, I will use those
            recordings only for personal purposes unless I obtain any consent required by Passage policy and applicable
            law for another use.
        </p>

        <h3>12. Service Animals and Animals</h3>
        <p>
            Animals are not permitted at Passage except service animals as required by applicable law. Service animals
            are subject to applicable legal standards and reasonable Event and venue safety requirements. Emotional
            support animals are not treated as service animals under the federal ADA and are not permitted unless
            another applicable law requires otherwise.
        </p>

        <h3>13. Governing Law; Severability; Entire Agreement</h3>
        <p>
            This Agreement is governed by the substantive laws of the State of Alabama, without regard to
            conflict-of-law principles. If any provision is found invalid or unenforceable, that provision shall be
            enforced to the maximum extent permitted by law or severed to the minimum extent necessary, and the
            remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.
        </p>

        <p>
            This Agreement, together with incorporated Event rules and policies expressly referenced herein, constitutes
            the entire agreement concerning the subjects addressed here and supersedes prior oral or written
            representations concerning those subjects. No oral statement may modify this Agreement. Any written
            modification must be authorized by the applicable parties.
        </p>

        <h3>14. Mediation First; Court Litigation in Montgomery County</h3>
        <p>
            Before filing a lawsuit arising out of or relating to this Agreement, Passage Gathering, the Event, the
            Facilities, or the Activities, the claimant and the applicable Releasee(s) shall first make a good-faith
            attempt to resolve the dispute through mediation in Montgomery County, Alabama. Mediation is a condition
            precedent to filing suit, except where emergency injunctive relief is reasonably necessary, a limitations
            period would otherwise expire, or applicable law prohibits enforcement of this requirement. Unless otherwise
            agreed in writing, the parties shall share the mediator’s fees equally and each party shall bear its own
            attorneys’ fees and costs incurred in mediation.
        </p>

        <p>
            If mediation does not resolve the dispute, any lawsuit shall be filed exclusively in a state or federal
            court of competent jurisdiction located in or serving Montgomery County, Alabama, and the parties consent to
            personal jurisdiction and venue there. Alabama substantive law shall apply. Nothing in this Section requires
            arbitration, and this Agreement does not waive the right to a jury trial except to the extent a valid,
            case-specific waiver is later made in accordance with applicable law.
        </p>

        <h3>15. Acknowledgment and Electronic Signature</h3>
        <form class="form" action="https://www.formbackend.com/f/96087132935f92fa" method="POST">
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="first-name">First Name</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="first-name" id="first-name" type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="last-name">Last Name</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="last-name" id="last-name" type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="date-of-birth">Date of Birth</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="date-of-birth" id="date-of-birth" type="date" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="email">Email</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="email" id="email" type="email" />
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide">
                <label class="label" for="address">Address</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="address" id="address" type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="field field--third">
                <label class="label" for="city">City</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="city" id="city" type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="field field--third">
                <label class="label" for="state">State</label>
                <select class="input input--select" name="state" id="state" required>
                    <option value="">Select a state</option>
                    {
                        states.map((state) => {
                            const [abbreviation, name] = Object.entries(state)[0];
                            return <option value={abbreviation}>{name}</option>;
                        })
                    }
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="field field--third">
                <label class="label" for="zip">ZIP</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="zip" id="zip" type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="emergency-contact-name">Emergency Contact Name</label>
                <input
                    class="input input--text"
                    required
                    name="emergency-contact-name"
                    id="emergency-contact-name"
                    type="text"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="emergency-contact-phone">Emergency Contact Phone</label>
                <input
                    class="input input--text"
                    required
                    name="emergency-contact-phone"
                    id="emergency-contact-phone"
                    type="tel"
                    inputmode="numeric"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="id-number">ID Number</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="id-number" id="id-number" type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="id-state">Issuing State</label>
                <select class="input input--select" name="id-state" id="id-state" required>
                    <option value="">Select a state</option>
                    {
                        states.map((state) => {
                            const [abbreviation, name] = Object.entries(state)[0];
                            return <option value={abbreviation}>{name}</option>;
                        })
                    }
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide">
                <label class="label" for="notes">Optional Notes</label>
                <textarea class="input input--text" name="notes" id="notes"></textarea>
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide">
                <p>BY SIGNING OR ELECTRONICALLY ACCEPTING THIS AGREEMENT, I ACKNOWLEDGE AND AGREE THAT:</p>
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-age"
                    id="confirm-age"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-age"
                    >I am at least 21 years old and have legal capacity to enter into this Agreement.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-opportunity"
                    id="confirm-opportunity"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-opportunity"
                    >I have had sufficient opportunity to read this entire Agreement and understand its terms.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-risks"
                    id="confirm-risks"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-risks"
                    >I understand the nature of the Activities and the Risks described in this Agreement and knowingly
                    and voluntarily assume the inherent Risks of attending Passage and participating in Activities.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-negligence"
                    id="confirm-negligence"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-negligence"
                    >I understand that Section 4 releases claims based on the ordinary negligence of the Releasees to
                    the maximum extent permitted by Alabama law, but does not purport to release wanton, willful, or
                    intentional misconduct or any other claim that cannot lawfully be waived.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-mediation"
                    id="confirm-mediation"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-mediation"
                    >I understand that disputes are subject to good-faith mediation first and, if unresolved, court
                    litigation in Montgomery County, Alabama; this Agreement does not require arbitration.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-policy"
                    id="confirm-policy"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-policy"
                    >I understand the ticket, cancellation, and force-majeure policy in Section 10 and that it controls
                    over any inconsistent refund statement.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-voluntary"
                    id="confirm-voluntary"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-voluntary"
                    >I am signing freely and voluntarily, without reliance on any oral promise that contradicts this
                    Agreement.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-electronic"
                    id="confirm-electronic"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-electronic"
                    >I agree that entering my name electronically, checking an acceptance box, or applying an electronic
                    signature constitutes my signature to the same extent as a handwritten signature, to the extent
                    permitted by applicable law.</label
                >
            </div>
            <div class="field field--wide field--has-checkbox">
                <input
                    class="input input--checkbox"
                    type="checkbox"
                    value="confirmed"
                    required
                    name="confirm-have-read"
                    id="confirm-have-read"
                />
                <label class="label label--prose" for="confirm-have-read"
                    >I HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THIS AGREEMENT AND SIGN IT VOLUNTARILY.</label
                >
            </div>

            <div class="field field--wide">
                <label class="label" for="signature">Electronic Signature / Typed Name</label>
                <input class="input input--text" required name="signature" id="signature" type="text" />
            </div>

            <button type="submit" class="btn">Submit</button>
        </form>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
    .container {
        max-width: 75ch;
        font-size: #{utils.makeClamp(14, 16)};
    }
    h2 {
        font-family: var(--ff-josefin-sans--regular);
        font-size: #{utils.makeClamp(24, 36)};
    }
    h3 {
        font-size: #{utils.makeClamp(18, 24)};
    }
    .form {
        display: grid;
        gap: 2em;
        @media (min-width: #{utils.getBreakpoint('lg')}) {
            grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
        }
    }
    .field {
        accent-color: white;
        @media (min-width: #{utils.getBreakpoint('lg')}) {
            grid-column: span 3;
            &--third {
                grid-column: span 2;
            }
            &--wide {
                grid-column: 1 / -1;
            }
        }
        &--has-checkbox {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 20px auto;
            gap: 1em;
            align-items: start;
        }
    }
    .input {
        &--select {
            border: 0;
            padding: 1em;
            width: 100%;
            background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.05);
            color: white;
        }
        &--text {
            border: 0;
            padding: 1em;
            width: 100%;
            background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.05);
            color: white;
        }
        &--checkbox {
        }
    }
    .label {
        font-size: #{utils.makeRem(14)};
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 1px;
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.75em;

        &--prose {
            text-transform: none;
            letter-spacing: 0;
            font-size: #{utils.makeRem(16)};
            margin: 0;
        }
    }
    input[type="date"]::-webkit-calendar-picker-indicator {
        filter: invert(1);
    }
</style>
